			"189": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "RING BUFFER & BUFFER [DATA]\n\nThe Ring Buffer and Buffer are two nodes that fill up a collection and releasing them under a set condition. \n\nThe Ring Buffer node fills up with values and once full it releases the values on a first-in-first-out basis. In addition to this the Ring Buffer can be manually reset and sends out a Boolean(TRUE) when it has been filled at least once since the last reset.\n\nThe Buffer node fills up and release all values when full.\n\nThis is demonstrated in the example patch. The same random values are assigned to both the Buffer and the Ring Buffer. The blue circles are placed by the Ring Buffer, first-in-first-out. The red circles are placed by the Buffer, once full all the circles jump.\n\nThe size of both nodes (how many values they hold) can be set in the inspector.\n\n"
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 783.70953369140625,
					"width": 1887.279541015625,
