			"192": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "RING BUFFER & BUFFER [TEXTURE]\n\nBoth the Ring Buffer and Buffer node support textures from Resolume 7.11 and on.\nThe concept stays the same, the Buffer collects X frames and sends them all out when full.\nThe Ring Buffer works on first-in-first-out basis, creating a smoother look\n\nIn this example both the Ring Buffer and Buffer hold 10 frames.\nKeep in mind that a single 8-bit 1920x1080 frame takes up about 8mb of VRAM(video memory) when buffered.\nThis is a \"with great power come great responsibiliy\" kinda deal."
					}
				},
